      "description": "Watch Al Ettifaq vs Al Nassr highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. On August 25, 2026 , the Pro League delivered a classic encounter between Al Ettifaq and Al Nassr . In a match defined by dramatic shifts in momentum, the contest provided a high-octane spectacle that kept spectators on the edge of their seats from the opening whistle to the final seconds. Early Crisis and Ettifaq Control The match took a shocking turn as early as the 13th minute when Al Nassr goalkeeper Bento Krepski was shown a straight red card. This forced the visitors into an immediate reshuffle, with Angelo Gabriel sacrificed for substitute keeper Abdulrahman Al Otaibi . Al Ettifaq wasted little time capitalizing on their numerical advantage, as Ondrej Duda found the net in the 31st minute to break the deadlock. As the first half drew to a close, things went from bad to worse for the visitors. Deep into stoppage time, Alvaro Medran struck a clinical second goal following an assist from Yasir Al Shammari . At 2-0 down and a man light, Al Nassr looked down and out as they headed into the tunnel. The Great Escape and Mane's Double The second half saw significant changes, with Cristiano Ronaldo substituted out as Al Nassr sought a way back. Despite the uphill battle and a yellow card for Joao Felix , the tide began to turn. In the 74th minute, Felix turned provider, setting up Sadio Mane to reduce the deficit and ignite hopes of a comeback. The momentum shifted entirely in a frantic three-minute spell. In the 77th minute, Joao Felix registered his second assist of the night, crossing for defender Abdulelah Al Amri to power home the equalizer. The home side, previously in total control, suddenly found themselves reeling under relentless pressure. The final act of this extraordinary drama arrived in the 90th minute. Sami Al-Najei played a decisive ball to Sadio Mane , who clinicaly finished to secure his second goal and complete an improbable turnaround. After a tense period of stoppage time, the final whistle confirmed a 3-2 victory for ten-man Al Nassr , marking one of the most resilient performances in the history of the competition."
